-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎮 1. RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is RLHF?

```text id="rlhf_def"
Training a model using human feedback to improve its responses
```

---

⚙️ RLHF Pipeline

```text id="rlhf_flow"
Pretrained Model → Human Feedback → Reward Model → PPO Optimization → Final Model
```

---

🔹 Steps in RLHF

1️⃣ Pretraining

Model learns from large text data

---

2️⃣ Human Feedback

Humans rank or score responses

---

3️⃣ Reward Model

Model learns what humans prefer

---

4️⃣ PPO Optimization

Model is fine-tuned using rewards

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Example

User asks:

```text id="rlhf_ex"
"Explain AI"
```

* Model gives multiple answers
* Humans choose best one
* Model learns preferred style

---

🎯 Benefits of RLHF

✔ Aligns AI with human values
✔ Improves response quality
✔ Reduces harmful outputs

---

⚠️ Challenges

❌ Expensive (requires human labeling)
❌ Subjective feedback
❌ Scaling difficulty

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔥 2. LLM Distillation

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Distillation?

```text id="distill_def"
Transfer knowledge from a large model (teacher) to a smaller model (student)
```

---

⚙️ How It Works

1️⃣ Train large model (teacher)
2️⃣ Use outputs to train smaller model
3️⃣ Student mimics teacher behavior

---

📊 Example

* GPT (large model) → teacher
* Smaller model → student

---

🎯 Benefits

✔ Smaller model size
✔ Faster inference
✔ Lower cost
✔ Easier deployment

---

⚠️ Limitations

❌ Some accuracy loss
❌ Less capability than original model

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚖️ 3. Constitutional AI

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Constitutional AI?

```text id="const_ai_def"
Training AI models using a set of predefined ethical principles
```

---

📜 Key Idea

Instead of only human feedback:

👉 Use **rules (constitution)** to guide AI behavior

---

📌 Example Principles

* Be helpful
* Avoid harmful content
* Be honest
* Respect user safety

---

⚙️ How It Works

1️⃣ Define rules (constitution)
2️⃣ Model generates responses
3️⃣ Model self-evaluates using rules
4️⃣ Improves output

---

🎯 Benefits

✔ Reduces harmful outputs
✔ Scalable (less human effort)
✔ More consistent behavior

---

⚠️ Challenges

❌ Defining perfect rules is hard
❌ May limit creativity
❌ Still evolving approach

